[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8030"] :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x+(-1)y+1z \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+(-1)z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-8031/selection/51d93b32a266e01e1e0060a3ac5b421c321d6262da723658b110de696ad98100" :answer/id #uuid "b35391ee-d931-5073-95d0-5fd4d27210c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8031/selection/208f242954b74ecf3fb3e00a2639c7b53577d8781aae717c251d21c79f58198e" :answer/id #uuid "a273ffed-c06d-5fae-8279-502007fedfaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8031/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "3c664da4-1f0f-5442-b313-f26aa7c80af3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8031/selection/a013c88b5ed3e954e56a519e7e6742d2a3484720ac920680832aa1bf4602553b" :answer/id #uuid "8f72370b-86f0-5a2a-9ab0-4dced685c99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 &