correct "q-8051/selection/780d317f34cab1664f6eff2a7db6c04bd46c3d0c6010a9cd3a42f205cc736c1d" :answer-field/choices ["q-8051/selection/2041515e39d109f29d85114d9a0cf9ba193744c372b0ecf8ad0d257cdbb615b5" "q-8051/selection/780d317f34cab1664f6eff2a7db6c04bd46c3d0c6010a9cd3a42f205cc736c1d" "q-8051/selection/798fef79a3e80043fcb475c4d3621a5d7ad317e01c2dc8dec3db908f01fbfa11" "q-8051/selection/dc844ac849a1c491cbfba13625ff6530248f5a01ea2ec82e1339dccd90f0b012" "q-8051/selection/98d1ea710d2610761256f35f9ae9bc1da9d6b279f8f1df0b7b5bb2656e7507a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8051" :question/id #uuid "4da5d90d-6879-535f-9e54-619a2c9e4a91" :question/math-academy-id "q-8051" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{4},$ where\n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}7x-3y \\\\ x-2y+z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $4\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x+(-3)y+0z \\\\ 1x+(-2)y+1z \\\\ 0x+0y+0z \\\\ 0x+0y+1z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x-3y \\\\ x-2y+z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8051/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e35b58a-530f-5b9b-8df2-eb737f8af581"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8051"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40450/selection/78261e5187704173aaa233c1ba5aece0b55e63d5b57b336b6f85c83414a43f9b" :answer/id #uuid "ae26d7e9-4745-5ffb-958d-8c106