c1f9-01d3-536d-a4af-1ceb8795cefe" :question/math-academy-id "q-97027" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97027/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97027"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140424/selection/f6c42494d8c6f55e7a5738248e6f1ff018fd9d84a5c3df051e87d529366e0549" :answer/id #uuid "0f4d085c-78b0-51df-b943-2961e39c6c20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}26 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140424/selection/51ff857b1c1118dc616bfb7ed9144830d9447cd1a5ea027896025b63164bc73b" :answer/id #uuid "f4745e08-59cb-55d0-b4a2-86d2a9c0ee83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140424/selection/381d3f50ac06bea8bb25c931457cf492ff6f6a209774ce8f0c406aa92872b770" :answer/id #uuid "6bc4f599-759a-55a2-b755-cede8639df51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ 25\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140424/selection/0afda3f32adfbbbb53100ab1984d43c5e3b263f348d5cab8193a5552aee831b0" :answer/id #uuid "e5907c55-befd-554b-8a83-e629b376573c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}26 \\\\ 17\\end{a