-140425/selection/e24b0ad7f5286a3c731d6e64adc51828ee4948a17eda5a6083792a8d3592dc76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140425" :question/id #uuid "e33fe2bb-6d66-5f91-becf-b6df459ced42" :question/math-academy-id "q-140425" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{4},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140425/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5901"] :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/81d01f5d724e8b9d186bc53a15b488868c5c2d5d661f09d7c1febd862011afba.png)" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/412113c303aa31d5a9c23d5b0fa45201a8803b96f5239b9b1d007fc5128413c9.png)\n\nNotice that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/bcd58c5310e4312fdbcc5619e0a89a03afb9bd5a6adff9a851e34d19e2bafb0b.png)\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/67da7147fc2e767f6c1fe15d2664d7f0b0e5f7b0778b168c6f702d2b999a2799.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5518"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/bfdf3147fb8488c3a0032f9dad326b5d8c3ff68be46738dc39215e5098af6272.png)\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/35814ac6d965ac688907d162b45d9b0b194ea40375d4e474466e4fb4b1de1c1b.png) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8x-5y \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ -4x+5y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5y-8x \\\\ -3x-6y \\\\ 5y-4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/f59824c26875665fcbd8adfc5414fa7b0c60254e01f725f9ca72cf1d370a3e8b.png)\n\nFinally, $a-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5519"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057898/assets/7a6d4db6774da29f9b89996e348fad61b281737db6b44e9a39efa016fa2f15f3.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
